        },
        {
            "title": "The Forward Pass Through a CNN Block",
            "description": "This level integrates the individual components into a single computational step. You will trace the data flow through a complete CNN block: an input feature map is transformed by a Convolutional layer, passed through a non-linear Activation function, and then downsampled by a Pooling layer to produce an output feature map. This establishes the foundational forward-pass logic for deeper networks."
        },
        {
            "title": "Architectural Composition: From Blocks to a Simple CNN",
            "description": "This final level synthesizes the concepts by constructing a full network diagram. You will learn how to stack multiple Convolution-Activation-Pooling blocks to form a simple, complete CNN architecture. The diagram will visualize the progressive reduction in spatial size and the increase in the number of feature maps (depth) as data moves deeper into the network, concluding with a transition to a final classifier."
